  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The ratio of molar specific heat capacity at constant pressure to the molar specific heat capacity at constant volume is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></math></p><p>where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi></math>&nbsp;is constant for a given gas.</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math></p>"
